  "query_preview": "forecast with deterministic models, as well as the \nLREF-ensemble clusters diverging with multiple potential \nsolutions that would result in a different forecast for east \ncentral Florida. Guidance is in fairly good agreement until \nWednesday into Thursday. Regardless, high pressure is expected to \nbuild to the north over the eastern CONUS with a gradual increase \nin temperatures and precipitation chances expected into the \nworkweek as onshore flow develops. Winds are expected to become \nbreezy from the northeast on Monday before becoming breezy to \nwindy on Thursday. Although there is a great deal of uncertainty\nin the forecast, there is also the potential for coastal impacts \nwith persistent onshore flow in place, especially mid to late \nweek. Moisture increases on Tuesday with isolated to scattered \n(~20-50% chance) onshore moving showers with scattered to numerous\nshowers and a low chance for lightning storms mid to late week. \nSeasonable to below normal temperatures are forecast on Monday \nwith likely seasonable to above normal temperatures into late \nweek.",
